---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { contactEmail, updated, legalName, jurisdiction, refundDays } from "../legal";
import { pageLd } from "../site";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const site = Astro.site?.href ?? "https://heyminnie.com/";

const h2 = "prose-h2";
const p = "prose-p";
const ul = "prose-ul";
const link = "prose-a";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Minnie for Mac"
  description="The agreement for using Minnie: a free licence, optional one-time purchases, and what you take responsibility for when an AI agent runs on your Mac."
  jsonLd={[pageLd({ url: new URL("terms/", site).href, name: "Terms of Service", description: "The agreement for using Minnie: a free licence, optional one-time purchases, and what you take responsibility for when an AI agent runs on your Mac.", site, type: "WebPage" })]}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Terms", href: `${base}terms/` }]}
>
  <Navbar />

  <main class="legal">
    <a href={base} class="legal__back mono">← back to home</a>

    <h1 class="legal__h1">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="legal__date mono">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p class={p} style="margin-top:28px;">
      These terms are the agreement between you and {legalName} ("we", "us") for the
      Minnie app and this website. Installing or using Minnie means you accept them.
      They are written to be read, not to be survived.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>What Minnie is</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Minnie is a macOS application that gives an AI agent a voice, a face, and the
      ability to do work on your Mac. She is an interface to an AI agent — she is not
      the AI model herself, and the quality of what the agent produces is not
      something we control.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Your licence</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Minnie is free. We grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence
      to use her, at no charge, on Macs that you own or control. You may not resell,
      sublicense, or redistribute the app, or any licence key that comes with a
      purchase, and you may not remove or work around its licensing checks.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Price</h2>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li><strong>Minnie is free for life</strong> — the app and everything she does, with no trial, no subscription and no card.</li>
      <li>Later we may offer <strong>optional extra characters</strong> — a look, moves and a voice of their own — as <strong>one-time purchases</strong>. Each shows its price before you buy. None is a subscription, and none renews.</li>
      <li>Nothing that is free today will be moved behind a payment.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class={p}>
      Refunds for purchases are covered by our <a class={link} href={`${base}refund/`}>Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a> — {refundDays} days, no reason needed.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>What you are responsible for</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      This is the part that matters most, so it is not buried. Minnie runs an AI agent
      on your Mac <strong>outside the macOS App Sandbox</strong>, with access to your
      files and the ability to run commands. She asks before risky actions and shows
      you what she is about to do — but you can approve those actions, and once
      approved they run for real.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>You are responsible for:</p>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>What you ask Minnie to do, and what you approve when she asks.</li>
      <li><strong>Keeping your own backups.</strong> An approved command can delete or overwrite files, and we cannot undo that.</li>
      <li>Having the rights to the files, accounts and tools you point her at.</li>
      <li>Your own accounts and API keys with AI, speech and tool providers, and complying with their terms.</li>
      <li>Using Minnie lawfully — not for anything illegal, not to attack or gain unauthorised access to systems, and not to build a competing product out of her.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class={h2}>AI output</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      AI agents get things wrong, confidently. Anything Minnie writes, summarises, or
      does can be inaccurate or unsuitable, and none of it is professional advice —
      legal, financial, medical or otherwise. Check work that matters before you rely
      on it, and be careful about approving actions you have not read.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Third-party services</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Minnie connects to services you choose — AI providers, speech providers, and
      tools you connect over MCP. Those are governed by their own terms, we do not
      control them, and we are not responsible for what they do, what they charge, or
      whether they stay available. If a provider changes or disappears, parts of
      Minnie that depend on it may stop working.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Beta builds</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Beta versions are provided as-is, may be unstable, carry an expiry date, and can
      be retired remotely when a newer build is required. Do not use a beta for
      anything you cannot afford to have go wrong.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Updates and changes</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Minnie can download and install her own updates. Features may be added, changed
      or removed as the product develops. If we ever discontinue Minnie entirely, we
      will give notice first.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Warranty</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Minnie is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind, express or implied,
      including fitness for a particular purpose and uninterrupted or error-free
      operation. Some jurisdictions do not allow certain exclusions — where that is
      the case, this clause applies only as far as the law permits, and your statutory
      consumer rights are unaffected.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Liability</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect, incidental or
      consequential loss, or for lost data, lost profits or lost time. Our total
      liability for any claim is limited to what you paid us in the twelve months
      before it arose. Nothing here limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Ending the agreement</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      You can stop using Minnie at any time. We may suspend or end access if these
      terms are seriously or repeatedly broken — for example licence-key abuse or
      using Minnie to attack other systems.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Governing law</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      These terms are governed by the laws of {jurisdiction}, and its courts have
      jurisdiction over any dispute. If you are a consumer elsewhere, this does not
      remove protections you have under your own local law.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      We may update these terms as Minnie changes. The date at the top always says
      when. Continuing to use Minnie after a change means you accept the new version;
      if you do not, you can stop using her at any time.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Contact</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Email <a class={link} href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> — a
      real person answers.
    </p>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
